; A file which stops in the middle of a node, which is what an interrupted write
; or a bad merge leaves behind.
;
; It is here for the fmt stage's other branch. A file which is merely not
; canonical has no line to report, because what is wrong with it is the whole
; file's shape; a file which does not parse carries a diagnostic with a span,
; and that span is the one the fmt filter has to read out of the output
; contract. Nothing in the model root beside this one exercises it, because a
; file which does not parse also stops the model loading — which is why this
; root exists apart from that one.
(node
  site:S-003
  (label "Meeting Room C"
  (kind Space)
